TITLE:: Patternarium Foundations
SUMMARY:: Four mechanisms for stateful stream computation
CATEGORIES:: Libraries>Patternarium
RELATED:: Guides/Patternarium

DESCRIPTION::
Use Pscan for one state output per input, Pwindow for bounded local neighborhoods, Ptransduce when output cardinality changes, and Pmorphism for parallel symbolic generations.
code::
Pscan(Pwindow(Pseries(1, 1, 6), 2).collect(_.sum), 0, _ + _).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Patternarium-Foundations / Value stream
var values = {
Pscan(Pwindow(Pseries(1, 1, 6), 2).collect(_.sum), 0, _ + _).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isArray) { x } { x*2 }, dur: 0.22, amp: 0.06)
}.play;
)
::
Every stream has local iteration state. A mutable initial state supplied as a literal is still caller-owned: use a Function returning a fresh object when transitions mutate it. Outputs are values, including Arrays and Events; they are not recursively embedded as Patterns.
